      "side": 1,
      "message": "The sysfs node is only created if the device supports the multi-platform feature.\n\nThis is for the case where peripheral claims to support the feature but reports that it is not configured for a particular OS (return value: 0xFF which Logitech defines as invalid). It is a bit unclear when the device firmware will return this value since there should be a default.\n\nIn the case where the peripheral reports OxFF/NODATA, a user could still write to the node to set the OS, at which point reading will return a valid value.",
